# Active workers Canvas (Cursor main agent)

When this Cursor chat is the **Sume main agent** and has (or just had)
background workers — Opus via `claude-human-stream`, Grok/Composer via
`Task` — keep a live board canvas updated.

## Canvas path

`~/.cursor/projects/<workspace-slug>/canvases/active-workers-board.canvas.tsx`

Example for `sume-com`:
`/Users/huhchaewon/.cursor/projects/Users-huhchaewon-sume-sume-com/canvases/active-workers-board.canvas.tsx`

Create it if missing (read `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/canvas/SKILL.md` first).
When you mention the board to the user, link that absolute `.canvas.tsx` path.

## When to refresh (same turn — do not skip)

Update the canvas whenever any of these happen:

1. **Launch** an Opus Shell or Grok/Composer `Task`
2. **Completion / abort** notification for a worker Shell or Task
3. **Steer / kill / resume** that changes which workers are live
4. User asks worker status (“터미널 뭐 돌아?”, “어때?”, board check)

Do the refresh in the **same turn** as the status/handoff reply — not as a
later nice-to-have. Keep it short: reconcile → rewrite canvas → brief chat.

## Truth source (anti-overcount)

Live count = intersection of:

- Cursor terminals with **alive PID** + still-running worker command
- Live `claude -p` / `claude-human-stream` processes (and live Grok Tasks)
- Recent `opus-live` logs only as enrichment — **not** as proof of liveness

Drop finished workers from the “live” table immediately (move to
“just finished” if useful). Stale terminal files marked `running` with no
process = omit.

## Columns to keep current

For each live worker: **Job title** (see below), terminal id, issue, started
(KST), elapsed, model (`Claude Opus` / `Fable` / `Grok 4.5 Task`), transport
(`Shell → claude-human-stream` vs Cursor Task), `session_id` / agent id,
PR URLs, latest log signal (“now”).

Snapshot timestamp in the canvas header. Board language: English is fine
(ops artifact); user chat stays in the user’s language.

## Job title = terminal title = board Job (Chase lock 2026-08-07)

Chase maps workers from the Cursor terminal list. Those rows use the Shell
tool’s **`description`** (stored as terminal `title`). The Active workers
board **Job** column must use the **same string**.

| Kind | Exact `description` / board Job |
|------|----------------------------------|
| Opus Shell | `Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)` |
| Opus, no issue yet | `Opus : <job-slug>` |
| Grok land / CI Task | `Grok : <job-slug> (#<issue>)` |
| Composer explore | `Explore : <job-slug>` (optional `#N`) |

Examples: `Opus : dashboard-ui-chrome (#2819)`,
`Grok : dashboard-ui-chrome (#2819)`.

- `--name` / Task slug stem stays the bare kebab (`dashboard-ui-chrome`).
- **Forbidden board/terminal labels:** prose (“Create arch mega-issue…”,
  “Relaunch dead #2820…”), command-comment leaks (`Cursor (# Reopen…)`).
- On resume/steer: keep the **same** title as the live job.

## Non-goals

- Not a substitute for completion-notification monitoring (still no
  `AwaitShell` poll loops).
- Do not block the turn on perfect design polish — accuracy of the live
  set beats pretty layout.
- Codex / Claude Code as main agent: ignore this rule (Cursor-only).
